{"name":"Bismarck","hex":"#486c7a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bismarck","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname of German origin.\n Otto von Bismarck, one of the prominent German statesmen of the nineteenth century.","Otto von Bismarck, one of the prominent German statesmen of the nineteenth century."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An apple cultivar from Australia.","Alternative form of bismarck."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bismarck"}],"entries":[{"title":"Otto von Bismarck","blocks":[{"text":"Otto Eduard Leopold, Prince of Bismarck, Count of Bismarck-Schönhausen, Duke of Lauenburg, was a German statesman and diplomat who oversaw the unification of Germany and served as its first chancellor from 1871 to 1890. Bismarck's Realpolitik and firm governance earned him the nickname Iron Chancellor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Otto_von_Bismarck_1885_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Otto_von_Bismarck_1885_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otto_von_Bismarck"},{"title":"Bismarck, North Dakota","blocks":[{"text":"Bismarck is the capital city of the U.S. state of North Dakota and the county seat of Burleigh County. It is the state's second-most populous city, after Fargo. The population was 73,622 at the 2020 census, and was estimated at 77,772 in 2024, while its metropolitan population was 133,626. In 2014, Forbes magazine ranked Bismarck as the seventh fastest-growing small city in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Bismarck%2C_North_Dakota_aerial_view.jpg/330px-Bismarck%2C_North_Dakota_aerial_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bismarck%2C_North_Dakota"},{"title":"Bismarck (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"The surname Bismarck is most often associated with Otto von Bismarck (1815–1898), a Prussian statesman and first Chancellor of Germany."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bismarck_(surname)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R68588%2C_Otto_von_Bismarck.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R68588%2C_Otto_von_Bismarck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R68588%2C_Otto_von_Bismarck.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R68588%2C_Otto_von_Bismarck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABundesarchiv_Bild_183-R68588%2C_Otto_von_Bismarck.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Otto_von_Bismarck%2C_Jugendbildnis_im_Alter_von_22_Jahren.jpg/500px-Otto_von_Bismarck%2C_Jugendbildnis_im_Alter_von_22_Jahren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Otto_von_Bismarck%2C_Jugendbildnis_im_Alter_von_22_Jahren.jpg/500px-Otto_von_Bismarck%2C_Jugendbildnis_im_Alter_von_22_Jahren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bismarck in 1833, at age 18","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOtto_von_Bismarck%2C_Jugendbildnis_im_Alter_von_22_Jahren.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/BismarckLandtag.jpg/500px-BismarckLandtag.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/BismarckLandtag.jpg/500px-BismarckLandtag.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bismarck in 1847, at age 32","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABismarckLandtag.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Bis